om the mouth of Brahma, and from his heart, the Pranava\nThe Ukar appeared.\nTasyooshnigasillombhyo Gayatri cha tvacho vibho.\nTrushmansatnu anushtuljagatyasthnah Prajapatih. 45). Meaning of the word:\nTasya--his/her; Ushnik--a Vedic meter; Asit--originated; Lomabhyah--from the hairs on the body; Gayatri--the main Vedic\nmeter; Cha--also; Tvacha--from the skin; Vibhoh--of the Lord; Trishthapa-a special type of meter; Mamsaat-from the flesh; Snutha-from the vein Om\nfrom; Anushtup-another meter; Jagati-another meter; IST: from the bones; Prajapatih--of the father of living beings;.\nThereafter, from the hairs of the body of the all-powerful Prajapati, the art of hotik, that is, literary expression,\nwas produced. The main Vedic mantra Gayatri originated from the skin of living beings, fg\nfrom their flesh, Anushtup from their veins, and Jagati Chhanda originated from their bones.\nMajanyaah panka rutanyanna vrhati pranato'bhavat. 46. Meaning of the word:\nMajnayaah--from the bone marrow; Panka--a special type of verse; Utpanna--begotten; Brihati--another type of verse;\nPranatah--from the life force; Abhavat--begotten..\nThe art of writing a line and verse originated from the bone marrow, and another verse, the grandiose,\nThe art of writing originated from the life force of the lords of living beings."},{"pageNumber":1776,"text":"378\nस्पर्शस्तस्याभवज्जीव: स्वरो देह उदाहत\nउष्माणमिन्द्रियाण्याहुरन्तःस्था बलमात्मनः |\nस्वराः सप्त विहारेण भवन्ति स्म प्रजापतेः ॥ ४७॥\nशब्दार्थं\n\nस्पर्शः-- क से म तक के अक्षरों का समूह; तस्य-उसका; अभवत्‌-- हुआ; जीवः-- आत्मा; स्वरः — स्वरः; देहः--उनका शरीर;\nउदाहतः -- व्यक्त किये जाते हैं; ऊष्माणम्‌--श, ष, स तथा ह अक्षर; इन्द्रियाणि--इन्द्रियाँ; आहुः-- कहलाते हैं; अन्तः-स्थाः--\nय, र, ल तथा व ये अन्तस्थ अक्षर हैं; बलम्‌-- शक्ति; आत्मनः--उसकाः; स्वराः- संगीत; सप्त- सात; विहारेण--ऐन्द्रिय\nकार्यकलाप के द्वारा; भवन्ति स्म- प्रकट हुए; प्रजापतेः — जीवों के स्वामी का ।.\n\nब्रह्मा की आत्मा स्पर्श अक्षरों के रूप में, उनका शरीर स्वरों के रूप मे,