 la and va, these are the last letters; Balam-- strength; Atmanah-- His; Swarah-- music; Sapta- seven; Viharena-- through the senses;\nBhavanti sma- appeared; Prajapatih-- of the lord of living beings..\n\nThe soul of Brahma, in the form of touch letters, their body in the form of vowels, their senses in the form of heat,\nIn the form of letters, their strength in the form of inner letters, and their fsa activities manifested as music.\nOf the seven notes. Note: Sanskrit has 13 vowels and 35 consonants. Vowels are-A MEI HF HEH TT\nT O. and O and consonants like khu gu ghu etc.\nIn dishes, the first 25 letters are called 'Sparsh'.\nThere are also four FEEs. FH HA three (sh, sh, s) are called palatal, cerebral, and dental. In music,\nthe notes are Sa Re, Ga Mu: Ae, Dha Ta Ni. These sounds are essentially called word-Brahma, that is, spiritual sound. Thus, it is said that the creation of Brahma took place in the Mahakalpa as an incarnation of Shabda Brahma. Veda\nThe word is Brahman, therefore there is no need to give a physical explanation of the sounds of Vedic literature.\nThere is no need. The pronunciation of the Vedas should be done in the same form in which they are, although they are symbolically represented to us by\nphysically known letters. Ultimately, nothing is physical, because\nevery object originates from the spiritual world. Therefore, the physical world is, in the proper sense, called attachment or delusion. For those who are self-realized, there is nothing besides the soul.\nHe is the one who is beyond the manifest and unmanifest, the self-existent, the unmanifest, and the manifest.\nHe shines forth, pervading all, and is adorned by various powers. 48>. Shabdartham\n\nShabda-Brahma - Divine Sound; Atmanah - Lord Krishna; Tasya - His; Vyakta - Manifest; Avyakta-Atmanah - Of the unmanifest; Parah - The Supreme; Divya - Divine; Brahma-Paramah - Supreme; Avabhati - Appearing; Vitatah - While distributing; Nana - Various; Shakti-Forces; Upavrhanah - Enriched; Sahit - Associated..\n\nBrahma is the embodiment of God in the form of divine sound, therefore they are manifest and unmanifest"},{"pageNumber":1777,"text":"379\n\nकी धारणा से परे | ब्रह्मा परम सत्य के पूर्ण रूप हैं ओर नानाविध शक्तियों से समन्वित हैं।\n\nतात्पर्य : ब्रह्मा का पद ब्रह्माण्ड भर में सबसे अधिक उत्तरदायित्वपूर्ण पद है। यह ब्रह्माण्ड के\nसर्वाधिक पूर्ण व्यक्ति को प्रदान किया जाता है। जब इस पद को ग्रहण करने के लिए उपयुक्त जीव नहीं\nमिलता तो भगवान्‌ को स्वयं ब्रह्मा बनना पड़ता है। भौतिक जगत में ब्रह्मा भगवान्‌ का पूर्ण प्रतिनिधित्व\nकरते हैं और प्रणव अर्थात्‌ दिव्य ध्वनि उन्हीं से आती है। इसीलिए वे विविध शक्तियों से समन्वित\nरहते हैं जिनसे ही इन्द्र, चन्द्र तथा वरुण जैसे सारे देवता प्रकट होते © | उनके दिव्य महत्त्व को कम\nनहीं आँका जाना चाहिए, यद्यपि उन्होंने अपनी ही पुत्री के साथ रमण करने की प्रवृत्ति प्रदर्शित की थी।\nब्रह्मा द्वारा ऐसी प्रवृत्ति के प्रदर्शन का एक अभिप्राय है और उन्हें सामान्य जीव की तरह गर्हित या\nनिन्दनीय नहीं मानना चाहिए।\nततोऽपरामुपादाय स सर्गाय मनो दधे ॥ ४९॥\n\nशब्दार्थ\n\nततः-- तत्पश्चात्‌; अपराम्‌-- अन्य; उपादाय — स्वीकार करके; सः-- वह; सर्गाय- सृष्टि विषयकः; मनः-- मन; दधे--ध्यान\nदिया।\n\nतत्पश्चात्‌ ब्रह्मा ने दूसरा शरीर धारण किया जिसमें यौन जीवन निषिद्ध नहीं था ओर इस तरह\nवे आगे सृष्टि के कार्य में लग गये।\n\nतात्पर्य : ब्रह्मा का पहला शरीर दिव्य था जिसमें यौनजीवन के प्रति अनुरक्ति वर्जित थी, अतएव\nयोन से सम्बद्ध होने के लिए उन्हें दूसरा शरीर अंगीकार करना पड़ा। इस तरह उन्होने सृजन कार्य में\nअपने को लगाया | उनका पूर्व शरीर कुहरे में बदल गया जैसाकि पहले वर्णन हो चुका © |\nऋषीणां भूरिवीर्याणामपि सर्गमविस्तृतम्‌ |\nज्ञात्वा तद्धृदये भूयश्चिन्तयामास कौरव ॥ ५०॥\n\nशब्दार्थ\n\nऋषीणाम्‌- ऋषियों का; भूरि-वीर्याणाम्‌--अत्यधिक पराक्रम से; अपि-- के बावजूद; सर्गम्‌- सृष्टि; अविस्तृतम्‌-- विस्तृत\nनहीं; ज्ञात्वा-- जानकर; तत्‌- वह; हदये--हृदय में; भूयः-- पुन; चिन्तयाम्‌ आस-- विचार करने लगा; कौरव --हे कुरुपुत्र \\.\n\nहे कुरुपुत्र, जब ब्रह्मा ने देखा कि अत्यन्त वीर्यवान ऋषियों के होते हुए भी जनसंख्या में\nपर्याप्त वृद्धि नहीं हुई तो वे गम्भीरतापूर्वक विचार करने लगे कि जनसंख्या किस तरह बढायी\nजाय।","textEn":"379\n\nBeyond the concept. Brahma is the complete form of the ultimate truth and is integrated with various powers. Meaning: The position of Brahma is the most responsible position in the universe. This is given to the most complete person in the universe. When a suitable being is not found to take this position,\nthen God himself has to become Brahma. In the physical world, Brahma represents the complete form of God,\nand the divine sound, Pranava, that is, the divine sound, comes from them. Therefore, they remain coordinated with various powers,\nfrom whom all the gods like Indra, Chandra, and Varuna manifest. Their divine importance should not\nbe underestimated, although they had shown a tendency to engage in intercourse with their own daughter. It is an indication of such a display of tendency by Brahma, and they should not be considered inferior or\nindecent like ordinary beings.\nThen, taking him up, he made him the mind of the world. 49). Meaning of the word\n\nTatah-- After that; Aparaam-- Other; Upaaday-- Having accepted; Sahah-- He; Sargaya- Related to creation; Manah-- Mind; Dadhe- Meditation\nGiven. Thereafter, Brahma assumed another body in which sexual life was not prohibited, and in this way,\nthey further engaged in the work of creation. Meaning: Brahma's first body was divine, in which attachment to sexual life was prohibited, therefore,\nto be associated with the womb, he had to accept a second body. In this way, he engaged himself in creative work.\nHis previous body transformed into mist, as described earlier.\nHaving known the great valor of the sages, he thought again in his heart, O Kauravas. 50>. Meaning of the word\n\nOf the sages--of the sages; Bhoori--from valor; Api--even though; Sargam--Creation; Avistritam--Extended;\nNot; Gnatva--Knowing; Tat--That; Hadaye--In the heart; Bhuyah--Again; Chintayaam-Aas--Started to think; Kauravas--Oh sons of Kuru \\.\nHey Kuruputra, 