\nMeaning of the word:\nOh--Hi; Adbhutam--It is wonderful; Etat--This; Me--For me; Vyaptasya--Being busy; Api--Although; Nityada--Always;\nNa--Not; Hi-Certainly; Utyannante-They are doing; Prajya--Living beings; Nunam--But; Daivam--Fate; Anra--Here; Vyaghatakam--\nOpposite, contrary.. It is a strange thing that even though I am spread everywhere,\nthe population in the universe is still insufficient. The reason for this misfortune is only fate's\nBeyond that, there is nothing else.\nAnd seeing the united creation, he looked at the divine.\nWhose form appeared in two ways, and what he sees. 52). Meaning of the word\nEvam--in this way; Yukta--thinking; Krutah--doing; Tasya--his; Daivam--divine power; Cha--also;\nAvekshatah--while watching; Tada--at that time; Kasya--the universe; Rupam--form; Abhuut--appeared; Daivedha--duplicate; Yat--which\nis; Kayam--his body; Abichakshate--is said..\nWhen they were so engrossed in thought and looking at the supernatural power, two\nother forms emerged from their body. They are still known as the form of Brahma's body. Meaning: From the body of Brahma, two bodies were produced. One had a frown and the other had an IW.\nChest. No one can tell the extent of their manifestation. That is why even today they are called\nwhich means the body of Brahma. From this, no information is obtained about their relationship as a son or daughter.\nNo information is obtained.\nFrom them, by the division of forms, the duality is achieved. 53 Meaning of the word\nTabhyam-- their; Roop-- form; Vibhagabhyam-- divided in this way; Mithunam-- sexual relations; Samapadyat-- to be completed properly;\nDone..\nThese two separated bodies became united with each other in sexual relations. He who is there, the best of men, the self-existent, the self-luminous."},{"pageNumber":1779,"text":"38.\nस्त्री यासीच्छतरूपाख्या महिष्यस्य महात्मनः ॥ ५४ ॥\nशब्दार्थ\nयः- जो; तु- लेकिन; तत्र-वहाँ; पुमान्‌- नर; सः-- वह; अभूत्‌-- बना; मनुः — मनुष्यजाति का पिता; स्वायम्भुवः —\nस