 man; Sah- he; Abhut- made; Manu- father of mankind; Swayambhuva-\nSwayambhuva named; Swa-rat- completely independent; Stri- woman; Ya- who; Aasit- was; Shatarupa- Shatarupa; Akhya- named;\nMahishi- queen; Asya- his; Mahatmanah- great soul;\nAmong these, the one who had the male form was called Swayambhuva Manu and the female Shatarupa was called\nKnown as the queen of Mahatma Manu. Then, in the Mithunadharma, the people became the best of warriors. 55>. Meaning of the word\nTada--At that time; Mithun--Sexual life; Dharmena--According to the rules; Prajaah--Sons; Hi--Certainly; Edham--Increased;\nhappened; Bhavuvira--Happened..\nThen they increased the population in successive generations by inbreeding.\nHaving touched the Shatarupa, he was born to the other nine wives.\nPriyatratottanapadau, three daughters were born to Bharata.\nAakuti, Devahruti, and Prasuti, thus the best. 56. Meaning of the word:\nSah-He (Manu); Cha-Also; Api-After; Shatarupayam-In Shatarupa; Pancha-Five; Apatyani-Sons; Ajijanat-\nBorn; Priyatrat-Priyavrata; Uttanapadau-Uttanapada; Tisakharah-Three; Kanyah-Daughter; Cha-Also; Bharat-Hey Bharat's son;\nAakutih-Aakuti; Devahutih-Devahuti; Cha-Also; Prasutih-Prasuti; Iti-Thus; Satam-Hey Sattam. Hey Bharatputra, when the time came, he (Manu) produced five children from Shatarupa, two sons\nPriyavrata and Uttanapada, and three daughters Akuti, Devahuti, and Prasuti.\nAkutim Ruchaye Pradatkarmay Tu Madhyamam.\nDakshayadatprasutim cha yat apuritam jagat. 57 Meaning of the word\nAakutim-- A girl named Aakuti; Ruchay-- To Ruchi Muni; Pradat-- Gave; Kardamay-- To Kardam Muni; Tu- But;\nMadhyamam-- Middle (Devahuti); Dakshay-- To Daksha; Adat-Gave; Prasutim- The youngest daughter; Ch- Also; Yat-From;\nFrom whom; Aapuritam- is full; Jagat- The whole world \\.\nFather Manu gave his first daughter Aakuti to Ruchi Muni, the middle daughter Devahuti to Kardam Muni\nand gave the youngest daughter Prasuti to Daksha. From them, the whole world was filled with population. Meaning: here is the history of the creation of the population of the universe. Brahmaji in the universe"},{"pageNumber":1780,"text":"382\nआदि जीवित प्राणी हैं जिनसे मनु स्वायंभुव तथा उनकी पत्नी शतरूपा उत्पन्न हुई। मनु से दो पुत्र तथा\nतीन पुत्रियाँ उत्पन्न हुई और उन सबों से आज तक विभिन्न लोकों की जन-संख्या उत्पन्न हुई है।\nइसलिए ब्रह्मा सबों के पितामह कहलाते हैं और भगवान्‌ ब्रह्मा के पिता होने से सारे जीवों के\nप्रपितामह कहलाते हैं | इसकी पुष्टि भगवद्गीता (११.३९) में इस प्रकार हुई है--\n\nवायुर्यमीऽग्नर्वरुणः TMG:\n\nप्रजापतिस्त्वं Friars |\n\nनमो नमस्तेऽस्तु FEAF:\n\nपुनश्च भूयोऽपि नमो नमस्ते ॥\n\n*' आप वायु के स्वामी, परम न्यायी यम, अग्नि तथा वर्षा के स्वामी हैं । आप चन्द्रमा हैं तथा आप\nप्रपितामह हैं । अतएव मैं आपको पुनः पुनः सादर नमस्कार करता हूँ।''\n\nइस प्रकार श्रीमद्भागवत के तृतीय स्कन्ध के अन्तर्गत “(कुमारं तथा अर्यो की सुटि ^“ नामक\nबारहवें अध्याय के भक्तिवेदान्त तात्पर्य पूर्ण हुए ।","textEn":"382\nThese are the first living beings from whom Manu, Swayambhuva, and his wife Shatarupa were born. From Manu, two sons and\nthree daughters were born, and from all of them, the population of various lands has been produced until today. Therefore, Brahma is called the father of all, and because God is the father of Brahma, all living beings\nare called the great-grandfathers. This is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita (11.39) as follows--\n\nVayu, Agni, and Varuna are the Tvam.\n\nPrajapati, you are the Friars.\n\nSalutations, salutations to you.\n\nAgain, salutations to you. *' You are the master of the wind, the supremely just Yama, the master of fire and rain. You are the moon and you are\nyour great-grandfather. Therefore, I greet you again and again.\"\n\nThus, under the third canto of Srimad Bhagavatam, the Bhakti Vedanta Tatparya is completed in the twelfth chapter named “(Kumaram tatha aryo ki suti ^“."}]}